                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why?  We should rely on AM4 in most cases.  That is actually human readable and understandable vs some random board part number.  \n\nWhen you rely on a part number we end up not having support for a new board variant, or you have to add all the new PVT part numbers here when we move to the PVT phase."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yang Chen",
                        "email": "yang.chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Quanta-YangChen"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't understand the rationale for this change.  Please put \"why\" in your commit messages and not just \"what\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yang Chen",
                        "email": "yang.chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Quanta-YangChen"
                    },
                    "message": "I removed the probe condition of the part number and only used the AM4 for the FCB."
                }
